I like cakes.
Now I need milk.
I walk down a long aisle.
I look at the shelf.
I can see the water and the juice.
But I cannot find the milk.
I look everywhere.
I see a man.
He works in the supermarket.
I stop the employee and smile.
"Excuse me," I say.
"I would like to have milk."
"Where is the milk?"
The man points to the back of the shop.
"The dairy section is down there," he says.
"Thank you very much," I reply.
I walk down there.
I finally find the fridge and the milk.
I take a carton and lay it in the basket.
